        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"247\") (name \"unconnected-(NAVC1-PB6-Pad58)\") (class \"Default\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "NAVC↔FCC run UART2 + I2C + GPIO between the two MCUs"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The navigation MCU is isolated from its sensors and from the flight-control MCU, so navigation data cannot be acquired or exchanged.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": [
        "FCC1",
        "HSE1",
        "C32",
        "C33",
        "R23"
      ],
      "pins": [
        "FCC1.5",
        "FCC1.37",
        "FCC1.12",
        "FCC1.13",
        "HSE1.1",
        "HSE1.3"
      ],
      "nets": [
        "HSE_IN_FCC",
        "HSE_OUT_FCC",
        "Net-(FCC1-PH0)",
        "VREF+_FCC"
      ],
      "observed": "The 25 MHz crystal is connected to FCC1 pins 5 and 37, which the library part names PE6 and PE7. The actual HSE oscillator pins PH0 and PH1 are instead left on unrelated nets: PH0 has only a capacitor to ground, and PH1 is tied into the VREF+_FCC net.",
      "expected": "The HSE crystal must connect to the STM32H753VITx HSE oscillator pins PH0 and PH1.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"31\") (name \"HSE_IN_FCC\") (class \"Default\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"PE6\") (pintype \"bidirectional\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"33\") (name \"HSE_OUT_FCC\") (class \"Default\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"37\") (pinfunction \"PE7\") (pintype \"bidirectional\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "HSE crystal (both MCUs) | FCC / NAVC | ABM8G-25.000MHZ-4Y-T3"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The external high-speed clock is not connected to the MCU HSE interface, so the FCC cannot use the intended 25 MHz HSE and timing-sensitive operation may fail.",
      "confidence": 0.88
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist shows multiple hard deviations from the intended Hades design: the 3V3 rail is split and not connected to the MCU/pull-up net, the NAVC MCU is disconnected from its sensors and FCC link, and the FCC HSE crystal is wired to non-HSE GPIO pins."
}

